{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you.</b> HaShem said to Moses: Lift your staff and split the sea before they journey forth, for He did not tell him to strike the sea, but only to stretch out his hand over the sea with the staff, in the manner of \"and Moses stretched out his staff over the heavens\" (Exodus 9:23). We know that the staff did not split the sea; rather, from the moment Moses stretched out his hand over the sea, HaShem would drive the sea with a fierce east wind, or the waters would split, for so it is written:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:24.859853509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}